1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,405
So what are we building? An assistant that looks and feels like ChatGPT,

2
00:00:04,405 --> 00:00:09,912
but runs entirely on one computer, inside the organization's own building,

3
00:00:09,912 --> 00:00:12,666
with no internet connection at all.

4
00:00:12,666 --> 00:00:16,520
It does four things that nobody else's version does.

5
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:20,926
One, it picks its own brain. We keep several AI models on the machine,

6
00:00:20,926 --> 00:00:26,433
and a small, fast program decides which one should answer, and then shows you why it decided that.

7
00:00:26,433 --> 00:00:31,389
Two, it finishes the job. Not a chat reply, an actual Word file,

8
00:00:31,389 --> 00:00:35,243
a spreadsheet, or a working program, saved to disk.

9
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:40,750
Three, it reads paper. Scanned reports, handwriting, photographs, engineering drawings,

10
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:46,257
and it shows you the exact patch of the page every fact came from.

11
00:00:46,257 --> 00:00:50,663
Four, it proves it is offline. We unplug the network cable and keep working.

12
00:00:50,663 --> 00:00:56,720
Then we press a button that deliberately tries to reach the internet, so you can watch it get blocked.
